        {
          "type": "turn_end",
          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto has built three AI agents:\n\n1. **Fraud Detection Agent** (offline evals, deployment next): Reviews newly published events and organizers on an event ticketing platform, recommending approve/reject/request-info with reasons. It auto-approves only on evidence verified in code; web sources can hold a decision back but never approve it. Offline evals show significant improvement: on a local 9B model, approved fraud fell from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations, and fraud approved without human review dropped from 27% to 0%. Claude Haiku 5.5 is chosen for deployment (86% accuracy vs 71%, 1% of fraud approved vs 8%). Stack: TypeScript, PostgreSQL, GCP.\n\n2. **Organizer Support Agent** (coming soon): Answers event organizers' questions about sales, payouts and setup without human review, pulling live data from PostgreSQL and the payments API. Stack: TypeScript, Tool calling, MCP, PostgreSQL.\n\n3. **Portfolio Agent** (personal project): An agent on his portfolio site that answers visitors' questions about his experience and projects in natural language. Also exposed as an MCP server so external agents can query it. Stack: TypeScript, Claude, MCP.",
            "toolCalls": [],
            "stopReason": "end_turn",
